WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.850
Two round pizzas.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:06.820
The first is thirty centimetres
across, cut into eight equal slices.

3
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.610
The second is twenty-four
centimetres across,

4
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.150
cut into six equal slices.

5
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.630
Lift one slice from each
and trace along the crust.

6
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.160
Bigger pizza, but more slices.

7
00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.690
So which slice gives you more crust?

8
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.100
Or are they exactly the same?

9
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:26.390
In this mission, you'll see
that a slice is a sector,

10
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.250
and the crust along its edge is an arc.

11
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.160
Arc length equals theta over
three hundred and sixty,

12
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.010
times two pi r.

13
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.290
So the crust depends on the angle
and the radius at the same time.

14
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:41.840
Your mission: decide which
slice has more crust,

15
00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:45.710
the thirty centimetre pizza's or
the twenty-four centimetre pizza's.
